  "details": [
   {
    "heading": "Conditions",
    "text": "You are a Combat Medic NCO operating in a field or deployed environment with casualties present. You are tasked to coordinate the evacuation of casualties for a supported maneuver element. As evacuation platforms become available, you will identify, direct and document casualty movement until all casualties are enroute to receiving facilities. You are provided with communications equipment, evacuation platforms (ground or air), established reporting formats (e.g., 9-Line and MIST), unit SOPs, medical doctrine (ATP 4-02.13), and a casualty collection point (CCP) with personnel available to assist. The operational environment includes potential threats, environmental constraints, and the need to synchronize with tactical leaders. This task should not be trained in MOPP 4."
   },
   {
    "heading": "Standards",
    "text": "Coordinate the evacuation of casualties in accordance with (IAW) ATP 4-02.13. Completeall performance steps with 100% accuracy, adhering to all performance steps, and utilizing GO/NO-GO criteria.Ensure proper documentation of treatment using DD Form 1380 TCCC Card or electronic medical records."
   }
  ],
